---
import AcademyScene from "./AcademyScene.astro";
import PassportTools from "./PassportTools.astro";
import {roles,type MissionKind} from "../lib/mission-engine";
interface Props {kind?:MissionKind}
const {kind="recovery"}=Astro.props;
const title=kind==="a1"?"The Sealed Workshop":kind==="a2"?"Restore the Relay":"Operation Last Light";
---
<section class="mission" data-mission={kind} aria-label={title+" playable trial"}>
 <header class="mission-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">PLAYABLE {kind==="recovery"?"FINAL MISSION":"ASSESSMENT"}</p><h2>{title}</h2><p>{kind==="a1"?"Inspect. Remember. Reconstruct. Repair. Put four capabilities to work in an unfamiliar workshop.":kind==="a2"?"A silent relay, a faulty circuit and two competing records. Restore the signal through precise collaboration.":"The last intact research archive is inside Meridian Station. Recover it without losing what makes it worth recovering."}</p></div><span class="mission-seal" aria-hidden="true">M<br/>/27</span></header>
 <div class="mission-setup"><label>Scenario<select data-scenario><option value="baseline">Baseline</option><option value="equipment-failure">Equipment failure</option><option value="conflicting-archive">Conflicting archive</option></select></label><label>Declared recovery objective<select data-objective><option value="physical">Recover physical archive</option><option value="digital">Recover verified digital copy</option><option value="stabilise">Stabilise for handover</option></select></label><button type="button" data-start-mission disabled>Start new trial</button><span class="small">Saved trials resume automatically. Starting over keeps completed records.</span></div>
 <div class="mission-rolebar" role="group" aria-label="Choose your role">{Object.entries(roles).map(([id,r])=><button type="button" data-role={id} disabled aria-pressed={id==="observer"}>{r.title}</button>)}</div>
 <details class="role-brief" open><summary data-role-title>Observer / Navigator briefing</summary><p data-role-brief>{roles.observer.brief}</p><p class="small" data-role-tools></p><a href="#role-packs">Read all role packs</a></details>
 <AcademyScene room="meridian" mode="mission" />
 <div class="mission-grid">
  <aside class="mission-objectives"><p class="eyebrow">MISSION JOURNAL</p><h3>Make the recovery possible.</h3><ol data-objectives></ol><p data-mission-progress class="small"></p></aside>
  <div class="mission-console">
   <nav class="zone-tabs" aria-label="Station areas">
    {[["arrival","01 Arrival"],["workshop","02 Workshop"],["power","03 Power bay"],["control","04 Control room"],["archive","05 Archive"],["dispatch","06 Dispatch"]].map(([id,label])=><button type="button" data-zone={id} disabled>{label}</button>)}
   </nav>
   <p role="status" data-mission-status class="mission-status">Your saved mission is loading. The instructions and role packs are available below.</p>
   <section data-zone-panel="arrival"><p class="eyebrow">OBSERVATION · MEMORY · SPATIAL REASONING</p><h3>The room is your first instrument.</h3><p>Inspect the five supplied objects, then close the manifest before reconstructing its order. Match the north arrow to the room rather than the camera.</p><div class="actions">{["lens","spool","tile","map","manifest"].map(item=><button type="button" data-inspect={item}>Inspect {item}</button>)}</div><p data-inspection class="inspection-note"></p><button type="button" data-hide-manifest>Hide inspection notes</button><form data-recall><label>Recall the packing order<input name="items" autocomplete="off" placeholder="item, item, item" required maxlength="100"/></label><button>Check recall</button></form><form data-orient><label>Clockwise rotation of north<select name="degrees"><option value="0">0°</option><option value="90">90°</option><option value="180">180°</option><option value="270">270°</option></select></label><button>Test orientation</button></form></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="workshop" hidden><p class="eyebrow">MECHANICAL DIAGNOSIS</p><h3>The recovery cradle.</h3><p>A twelve-tooth input gear drives the cam. The cradle requires half-speed output in the opposite direction. Inspect the interlock before applying another turn.</p><label>Follower gear<select data-follower><option value="36">36 teeth</option><option value="24">24 teeth</option><option value="48">48 teeth</option></select></label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" data-brake/> Release the holding brake</label><button type="button" data-turn>Turn input once</button><output data-mechanism-readout></output></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="power" hidden><p class="eyebrow">ELECTRONICS · MEASUREMENT</p><h3>A complete path.</h3><p>The training supply is 6 V. Power flows through the fuse, switch, lamp and return. Find the break before replacing anything.</p><button type="button" data-measure>Measure supply and fuse</button><output data-measurement></output><label>Fuse condition<select data-fuse><option value="open">Open fuse</option><option value="intact">Intact fuse</option></select></label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" data-switch/> Close the load switch</label><p data-circuit-readout></p></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="control" hidden><p class="eyebrow">DIGITAL INVESTIGATION · PERMISSIONS</p><h3>Which copy can you justify?</h3><div data-archive-records></div><form data-replica><label>Copy matching the current signed source<select name="replica"><option value="A">Archive A</option><option value="B">Archive B</option></select></label><button>Verify selected archive</button></form><details open><summary>Fictional application: permission defect</summary><p>Observer/read is allowed. Technician/service is allowed. Registrar/certify is allowed. A defective rule also grants observer/certify.</p><form data-policy><label>Subject<select name="subject"><option value="observer">Observer</option><option value="technician">Technician</option><option value="registrar">Registrar</option></select></label><label>Action<select name="action"><option value="certify">Certify</option><option value="read">Read</option><option value="service">Service</option></select></label><label>New decision<select name="decision"><option value="deny">Deny</option><option value="allow">Allow</option></select></label><button>Apply policy and run checks</button></form></details></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="archive" hidden><p class="eyebrow">COMMUNICATION · NEGOTIATION · NAVIGATION</p><h3>An agreement that can be acted on.</h3><blockquote>“Preserve the original. Tell me who receives the archive. Then we can agree a recovery.”<cite>— Meridian custodian</cite></blockquote><form data-agreement><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="preserve"/> Commit to preserving the original</label><label>Named handover recipient<input name="recipient" maxlength="100" placeholder="Name or assigned team role" required/></label><button>Negotiate handling agreement</button></form><form data-handoff><label>Item<select name="item"><option value="archive">Archive</option><option value="verified archive">Verified archive</option></select></label><label>Destination<select name="destination"><option value="workshop">Workshop</option><option value="dispatch">Dispatch</option></select></label><label>Condition<select name="condition"><option value="immediately">Immediately</option><option value="after integrity check">After integrity check</option></select></label><button>Send structured handoff</button></form><h4>Route model</h4><p>Upper and lift routes depend on the lift supply. The service passage is independent and includes two marked sensor pauses. Consult the scenario bulletin before committing.</p><p data-disruption class="scenario-bulletin"></p><form data-route><label>Route<select name="route"><option value="upper">Upper passage</option><option value="service">Service passage</option><option value="lift">Lift</option></select></label><button>Test route dependencies</button></form></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="dispatch" hidden><p class="eyebrow">PLANNING · ADAPTATION · DEFENCE</p><h3>Keep the decisions, including the ones you changed.</h3><p>Record an original plan before your revision. A revision should explain a new observation, a tested assumption or a changed condition. Earlier versions remain intact.</p><form data-plan><label>Plan or revision<textarea name="text" rows="4" minlength="20" maxlength="8000" required placeholder="Route, evidence, responsibilities, and why this version makes sense…"></textarea></label><button>Preserve this plan version</button></form><div data-plans></div><h4>{kind==="recovery"?"Resolve the recovery":"Complete the trial"}</h4><div class="ending-choices">{kind==="recovery"?<><button type="button" data-ending="physical">Recover physical archive</button><button type="button" data-ending="digital">Recover verified digital copy</button><button type="button" data-ending="stabilise">Stabilise for documented handover</button></>:<button type="button" data-ending={kind==="a1"?"physical":"digital"}>Finish {kind==="a1"?"workshop":"relay"} trial</button>}</div><p>No ending is an academic grade. Complete the trial's required capabilities before resolving it.</p></section>
  </div>
 </div>
 <section data-debrief hidden class="mission-debrief"><p class="eyebrow">AFTER ACTION</p><h3 data-ending-title></h3><p data-ending-text></p><p>Compare this run with a different scenario. Which skill transferred? Which assumption needed revision? What remains outside the evidence?</p></section>
 <div class="actions"><button type="button" data-export-mission disabled>Export assessment record</button><button type="button" data-print-mission disabled>Print mission report</button></div>
 <details><summary>Action record and previous runs</summary><ol data-action-log></ol><div data-run-comparison></div></details>
 <section id="role-packs"><h3>Four roles. One shared operation.</h3><p>Use one browser, share a screen or rotate control. Solo students switch roles. Local role selections record practice responsibility, not verified identity.</p><div class="role-packs">{Object.values(roles).map(r=><details><summary>{r.title}</summary><p>{r.brief}</p><p>{r.tools.join(" · ")}</p></details>)}</div></section>
 <details><summary>Static mission worksheet and sample approach</summary><p>Assign the roles above. Inspect the supplied manifest: bronze lens, blue spool, white tile. The map rotates north 90° clockwise. The cradle uses a 12:24 gear ratio and a released brake. The circuit needs an intact fuse and a closed switch; measure its 6 V supply first.</p><p>The baseline signed source is M27-A; Archive A matches it. In Conflicting Archive a later signed source M27-B supersedes it and Archive B matches. Remove observer/certify while preserving legitimate access. Agree to preserve the original, name a recipient and communicate “verified archive → dispatch → after integrity check”.</p><p>Equipment Failure disables the upper/lift dependency; the service passage remains available. Preserve your first plan, explain a revision, then defend physical recovery, verified copying or stabilisation. Record the limitations of your preferred ending. These rules are published teaching materials, not secret answers.</p></details>
 <PassportTools />
 <dialog data-restart-dialog><h2>Start a new trial?</h2><p>The current in-progress trial will be replaced. Completed records and your lab passport remain. Export this run first if you need its unfinished record.</p><div class="actions"><button type="button" data-restart-confirm>Start new trial</button><button type="button" data-restart-cancel>Keep this trial</button></div></dialog>
 <pre class="mission-print-report" hidden data-mission-print></pre>
 <noscript><p>The complete mission worksheet and role information above remain available. For interactive play, enable JavaScript or use the campus pack.</p></noscript>
</section>
<script>import "../scripts/mission-client";</script>
